From 512568fb1da37177a0f6a0aa23709b23a10e25f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sunwoong Joo <gomida@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 21:14:41 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] headless, base, blink, media: deterministic renderer
 entropy, unsupported-API detection, review fixes

Patches 9 (partial) and 10 of the deterministic capture series, plus the
fixes from the code review of patches 6-8.

Entropy (patch 9): base::subtle::SetRandBytesOverride in the new header
base/rand_util_deterministic_capture.h (rand_util.h untouched) lets a
--deterministic-capture renderer replace the OS entropy source behind
base::RandBytes with a seeded xoshiro256** stream
(--deterministic-capture-seed, default 1); crypto.getRandomValues,
crypto.randomUUID and the renderer's UUIDs repeat run to run. Blob URL
identifiers are minted in the browser process and still vary.

Unsupported APIs (patch 10): CaptureAgent observes use counters
(DidObserveNewFeatureUsage) for getUserMedia, getDisplayMedia,
RTCPeerConnection, MediaRecorder, EncryptedMedia, captureStream, WebCodecs,
WebGPU, ServiceWorker, SharedWorker and setSinkId; UseCounterImpl notifies the
frame client for file:// and about: documents in capture mode (only http(s)
did). Each API is reported once per document as a warning, or as the error
UnsupportedApiUsed when media.failOnUnsupportedApi is true (default).

Review fixes:
- WebMediaPlayerImpl releases the virtual-time pauser on OnError, treats an
  errored network state as stable and gives up a hold after 20 s real time, so
  a failed or stalled pipeline cannot freeze the renderer's clock.
- AudioRendererImpl keeps the capture sink for muted elements instead of the
  real-time null sink (the sink applies the volume), never waits for decoded
  audio on the media thread itself, and creates its weak pointer on the media
  thread.
- CaptureAudioEngine holds scoped_refptrs to its sinks; a sink leaves the
  list in Stop(), not in its destructor; the engine lock is never taken under
  a sink lock; the volume is an atomic.
- VideoRendererImpl reads past the soft buffering cap while a capture wait
  needs more frames (sources faster than three times the capture rate).
- CaptureSession counts audio sample frames only when the ring slot was
  written, keeps the resolved markers/media/audio defaults in the effective
  configuration, and sizes the prepare timer for the renderer's worst case.
- RawFrameSink validates the slot geometry including the audio area.
- Patch version 2.1.0-p10.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
